(project pricklypear-agent-native
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: agent-native — server-resident agent identities as first-class habitat inhabitants. A bot user (auth 008) wakes on cron, scans its rooms, decides, acts through the prim seam under its OWN identity, posts back, and pushes human attention out via ntfy. Rooms are member-gated data.s.<space>.* compartments (branching.shared-data-spaces); the loop seam is the shared llm/ Loop.host (prim-seam); notify.borg owns the push spec. The local counterpart is glochid (agent.borg): same seam, different residence — the native agent lives in the image's request loop, glochid lives on the laptop. Milestones: M1 wake loop (shipped 2026-09-03), M2 tool loop + promote gate, M3 ntfy push, M4 glochid pairing, M5 dogfood.")
 (status partial)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04 chapter created, plan-phase spec (roerick + gregor). Sources: the habitat note agent-native-design (2026-09-03, admin garden) + the M1 build it drove; substrate decision ace26b5 (branching.shared-data-spaces) — the shared-write-surface path, adopted over org-level branches (they cost nothing on the data plane, so they buy nothing), local-first federation (offline machinery for online server-resident identities), and agents-auth-as-the-human (attribution collapse + lost human-in-the-loop for more than one agent). Ownership line, same discipline as the prim-seam rename: this chapter owns the native-agent LOOP, identities, and rooms wiring; it does NOT re-spec the mechanisms it stands on — identities are multi-user/auth 008, the room substrate is branching.shared-data-spaces (S1-S3), wake scheduling is jobs, the prim surface is prim-seam (/api/prim refuse-or-forward, identity-scoped data plane), push is notify (its v1 IS ntfy-from-a-schedule; M3 is wiring triggers, not a new mechanism).|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-03 M1 RECORD (verbatim from the build, including the gotchas that cost hours — keep): bot user agent-prickle (uuid 09ee80ce-d543-426e-a005-9b740e9df113, 008_agent_users); token in ~/.config/pricklypear/env-agent-prickle (mode 600, never committed). Defines on agent-prickle/personal (branch-durable, top-level): agent/room, agent/bot, agent/seed, agent/scan, agent/find-room-row, agent/has?, agent/collect, agent/reverse, agent/last-id, agent/after, agent/notbot, agent/join, agent/state, agent/wake. Room agent-lab: CONVENTION membership (admin + gregor + agent-prickle list in an agent/room define) over author-scoped rows, so cross-user visibility does NOT really exist until shared-data-spaces S1/S2 land; enforcing it is this chapter's rooms milestone. State row: type agent-state, kind=wake, fields sid + cursor (last-processed row id). Schedule agent-wake cron */2, fn agent/wake, args "[]", runs as agent-prickle. VERIFIED: manual wake reply posted as agent-prickle; quiet tick makes NO provider call; cron tick fired on schedule and posted CRON-OK (job done, runner boot-80699). GOTCHAS (cost hours): /api/eval Basic auth is broken (401) — Bearer works for /api/eval AND /api/agent; admin auths via POST /login form fields + cookie, not Basic; schedule args must be the zero-arg convention "[]" — "{}" splices into the call source and evals unbound (dead jobs); defines persist ONLY as top-level eval exprs (a (seq ...) wrap evaluates but persists nothing); data_rows order is insertion order (chronological); fields.created_at is only what you write (chat lib wrote "").|) *)

 (section identities
  (doc "A native agent is a real user: an auth 008 bot user with a token, ONE personal branch that is both its code and its memory, and the same data plane and RLS as any human. Attribution is free: data_rows.author is the session username on every write. The agent never auths as anyone else; there is no sudo on the data plane.")
  (implements "migrations/008_agent_users.sql" "image/lib/auth_store.ml")
  (status partial)
  (* agent note (|2026-09-04: M1 shipped the first instance (agent-prickle), created by hand. Partial, not implemented: no provisioning story (create bot user + token + personal branch in one step), no token rotation, no per-agent tool namespace on the branch. Next concrete need (M2): a second bot user to prove the story generalizes before rooms make membership meaningful.|) *)
  (verify
   (test "a bot user attaches to its own personal branch exactly like a human session: kernel prim catalog + lazy env + staleness stamp identical")
   (test "writes attribute author=agent-prickle on data_rows and function_defs with no special casing"))
 )

 (section rooms
  (doc "Rooms are the native agent's shared surface: one named space per room (data.s.<room>.*), membership in data_space_members, RLS-enforced visibility — a member sees the union of members' space rows with per-row author; a non-member sees nothing. A message is an ordinary typed datum (room-message) under the space; tree-time versions destructive edits (before-images with author). M1's convention-membership room (agent-lab) is the seed this upgrades: same defines, enforced visibility once S1/S2 land.")
  (implements "borge/branching.borg shared-data-spaces S1-S3" "libs/agent")
  (status partial)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-08 RECONCILE + FIRST LIVE CONSUMER (deploy d1d4d4e, prod): the rooms substrate changed under this section — OPEN SPACES (branching.shared-data-spaces 09-06 note) made 'every authenticated identity is implicitly a member' a first-class space kind, and the FIRST consumer is the chat lobby: the bot's room is no longer a member-gated agent-lab but the OPEN chat-lobby space (libs/chat chat/ensure-space; room_id "lobby", rows in data.s.chat-lobby.*). LIVENESS VERIFIED END-TO-END ON PROD: deploy d1d4d4e -> reseed-package chat + agent onto system/main -> chat/ensure-space + chat/ensure-lobby bootstrapped the space -> agent lib upserted onto agent-prickle/personal (retiring the stale 20-form pins in place; load-library as admin on the checked-out bot branch) -> cron tick ran the new wake on lobby -> agent posted "I see messages. I'm reading the lobby." carrying wake_id lobby-<cursor> — cross-identity proof: the bot read admin-authored rows through the open space and replied as itself. agent/rooms repointed agent-lab -> lobby (old room rows are stranded pre-spaces per-user data; left in place). What keeps this PARTIAL rather than implemented: DM row-level routing stays v2; per-room membership management has no surface (open spaces need none — that is the point); libs/agent reached main via admin reseed-package, not a promote-review surface (the S4 gate below stays open).|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04: blocked on branching.shared-data-spaces S1/S2 (migration data_spaces + data_space_members + RLS disjunct; space-admit routing). Conventions recorded NOW so M2 does not relitigate them: transcript order is insertion order (data_rows); agent-posted messages carry the author's wake-id field (idempotency key, see tool-loop); created_at is written by the room lib ((now) epoch, shipped 09-04; the note's earlier "time-now" name was wrong - the prim is (now)); a member's read cursor lives in its OWN data.u.<agent>.* (the agent-state row), never in the room - cursors are per-reader state, not shared data. Promotion: the room lib moves from personal pins to the seeded libs/agent package via the normal human promote gate; the obituary note lands in spec/agent DECISIONS.|) *)
  (verify
   (test "after S1/S2: two member agents + admin see the same agent-lab rows; a non-member bot's scan returns nothing (RLS-enforced, not view-filtered)")
   (test "room/scan since-cursor returns rows newest-first with author + wake-id intact")
   (smoke "libs/agent seeded; agent-prickle's personal pins for room plumbing retired"))
 )

 (section wake-loop
  (doc "The heartbeat: a jobs cron schedule per agent (runs ON the agent's branch, as the agent) calls agent/wake. Quiet tick: scan the rooms, advance nothing, post nothing, NO provider call. Loud tick: something new since the cursor — build a bounded observation (last N rows), decide with one LLM call (ai_store session via /api/agent, max_steps small), post the reply, advance the cursor. M1 shipped this for one room with a hand-rolled scan/collect; M2 generalizes it into the tool loop below.")
  (implements "borge/jobs.borg" "libs/agent")
  (status partial)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04: M1 is the single-room quiet/loud wake, verified end to end (cron tick + CRON-OK + idempotent quiet paths). 09-04: the generalize slice SHIPPED as part of M2 - multi-room scan via agent/rooms, one state row per room with per-room cursors, observation parameterized by room (agent/room-msgs find-rows, no more 400-row global scan); M1's single-room state row deleted, its defines superseded by the tool-loop set.|) *)
  (verify
   (test "quiet tick on an up-to-date room makes no provider call and writes no rows (idempotent, observed 09-03)")
   (test "a room row arriving between ticks produces exactly one reply on the next tick"))
 )

 (section tool-loop
  (doc "M2: the wake becomes a LOOP. observe (room scan since cursor + own state) then decide (llm/ Loop.host over the shared seam; session in ai_store via /api/agent) then act (prims through /api/prim under the agent's own identity, refuse-or-forward classification inherited from prim-seam) then post (room-message stamped with the wake-id) then advance (cursor). Budgets are real: max_steps from /api/agent caps provider turns; the eval budget (400k steps, 2026-09-03) caps any single eval; the request gate bounds wall time.")
  (implements "borge/prim-seam.borg" "borge/lisp-interpreter.borg budgets" "lisp/lib/eval.ml" "image/lib/http.ml")
  (status partial)
  (* agent note (|2026-09-08 WAKE QUARANTINE + PARSE FLOOR (deploy d1d4d4e): the retry policy in the 09-04 note is amended — a deterministic provider failure used to pin the cursor forever (fail -> no advance -> cron retries every 2 min; observed 50+ identical failures on prod). Two fixes: (1) PARSE FLOOR — llm_codec surfaces provider error bodies (choices:null / error object) as "provider error: <message>" instead of bare Type_error, and Openai.complete maps parse failures to Error results, so the bounded failure note now names the real cause (first live diagnosis: the old agent-lab ai-session had grown to 200,705 tokens -> provider 400 context overflow; the new lobby state row mints a fresh session). (2) QUARANTINE — agent-state rows carry a "fails" marker; 3 consecutive failures on an unadvanced cursor advance past the poison message, push one "wake quarantined" ntfy, and reset; any cursor advance clears the marker. Verified on dev (forced failures via bogus sid: fail, fail, quarantined, quiet) and live on prod (wake -> lobby: posted). OPEN: the ai-session growth that caused the original wedge needs its own mechanism (session rotation/compaction) — filed in the habitat log/issues.|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04: the three decisions that make the loop safe to run unattended. (1) IDEMPOTENCY: the cursor is DERIVED from the transcript (max processed row id), and every post carries the wake-id, so a crash between post and advance replays the scan and dedupes instead of double-posting; a reposted wake-id is skipped by the room lib. (2) TRANSACTIONS: /api/eval is transactional — a failed wake rolls back clean; the jobs runner records the error and the next tick retries; no partial room state is possible. (3) TOOL GATE: the agent may register tools (register-tool) and install them on ITS OWN branch; anything destined for shared/system/main goes through the normal promote, which is HUMAN — the agent can propose (a branch + a note), never merge. Server-only prims stay refused for the agent surface exactly as for any prim-seam client (classification from register_server_only, never a hand list); loop default deny-list: checkout, branch forks/merges, promote, auth/session prims.|) *)
  (* agent note (|2026-09-04 M2 BUILT on agent-prickle/personal (13 top-level defines; promotion proposal at libs/agent/lib.pp, human gate pending): multi-room wake from agent/rooms config, one agent-state row per room (kind=wake, room/sid/cursor), per-room find-rows scan; deterministic wake-id = room-cursor stamped on every reply, so a crash between post and advance replays quietly (verified live: rewound cursor -> replay-quiet, no provider call, no double post); reply advances the cursor to its OWN row id; provider failure (agent error / max steps / no-session) returns a bounded note WITHOUT advancing - next tick retries, nothing lost; per-room guard isolates one room's error while Budget_exceeded intentionally propagates (transactional abort); created_at now written ((now)) epoch per the rooms convention. Gates verified live as the agent: promote-to-main denied (kind denied), install-function lands on the agent's own branch and runs (agent/selftest-double, author agent:<model>), /api/prim checkout refuses with the structured server_only error while in-eval checkout runs and is denied by branch ownership (prim-seam: same visibility in-process as proxied). Cron tick ran the v2 defines clean (agent-lab: quiet, runner boot-18999). OBSERVED rooms blocker, live probe: find-rows chat-message is author-scoped BOTH directions (gregor sees 1 row = his own; agent-prickle sees 11 = its own-authored rows; M1's from=gregor/admin rows were bot-authored mimic seeds) - human->bot room delivery waits on branching.shared-data-spaces S1/S2.|) *)
  (verify
   (build "dune build @all")
   (test "loop unit: wake with a canned provider reply posts exactly one room-message carrying the wake-id and advances the cursor")
   (test "crash between post and advance: next wake re-scans, sees the posted wake-id, posts nothing new")
   (test "budget: a reply path that exceeds max_steps or the eval budget stops, posts a bounded failure note, no runaway loop")
   (test "tool gate: an agent-installed tool lands on the agent's personal branch; an agent-initiated promote attempt errors (requires admin)")
   (test "server-only prims refused for the agent surface with the structured server_only error (same as any prim-seam client)"))
 )

 (section push
  (doc "M3: outbound human attention. The spec is notify.borg (its v1 IS server-push via ntfy from a jobs schedule; the trigger-split is recorded there). This chapter only wires the native-agent triggers: room mention of a member human, wake failure (the loop could not complete), tool proposal ready for promote review. Delivery failure logs and retries next wake; it never fails the wake itself. No inbound: waking stays cron + a human's reply (an agent never listens on a socket).")
  (implements "borge/notify.borg" "image/lib/prims_net.ml")
  (status partial)
  (* agent note (|2026-09-05 M3 WIRED (correction to the 09-04 note: http-post SHIPS - the real gap was the outbound gate's identity check: is_admin || username ends "/agent", which the auth-008 bot agent-prickle never matches). Two triggers live on agent-prickle/personal: room mention of a member human (agent/humans = admin + gregor, loose substring v1, one push per mention row via agent/notify-talk) and wake failure (provider max-steps/error pushes a wake-failed note); the tool-proposal trigger is DEFERRED - no proposal surface exists yet (promote-to-main is the only path and it is admin-only). ntfy-config row is BOT-OWNED (author=agent-prickle: author-scoped reads mean an admin-authored row would be invisible to the bot; the topic is a capability, kept in ~/.config/pricklypear/env-agent-ntfy mode 600 on vultr.guest, never in chat or git). DELIVERY VERIFIED LIVE: the 01:20Z cron tick pushed a mention to the topic and a submit-job probe pushed again - the jobs runner PASSES the outbound-http gate while direct /api/eval http-post is denied for the bot; agent/notify wraps every push in guard so notifications never fail the wake (denied pushes surface as bounded notify-error strings in the wake result). Kernel patch on branch agent-native-m2 (prims_net.ml is_admin_or_agent also honors user_type='agent' via Auth_store.get_user_by_username, deny-closed on lookup failure; compile-checked best-effort on wyo - its wyo-ocaml switch lacks lwt_eio and ocaml>=5.1 that the mainframe build uses, the two build errors there were environmental, in other files). PENDING ROERICK: push the kernel patch + one SQL flip (UPDATE users SET user_type='agent', parent_user_id=<admin> WHERE username='agent-prickle') to open the direct path; the flip has no admin API yet (post_admin_users has create_agent/revoke/issue/rotate but no type flip). KERNEL FINDINGS: (a) PP http-post drops custom headers on the POST path - body delivers, Title does not (local curl with the same header shows title on the same topic); (b) define persistence: a 4.6KB single-line define silently failed to persist twice while 2-4KB defines persisted - worth a look; (c) known race: a manual wake concurrent with a cron tick double-scans (two replies posted 01:19-01:20Z; wake-id dedupe catches replays, not races).|) *)
  (verify
   (smoke "a room mention pushes to the member's ntfy topic within seconds of the wake that saw it")
   (test "notify failure (network down) logs, does not fail the wake, retries next tick"))
 )

 (section glochid-pairing
  (doc "M4/M5: the native agent and glochid are one identity story from two residences. glochid (agent.borg) works its local lens and syncs; the native agent lives server-side and acts through /api/prim. Pairing means shared state conventions (same agent-state shape, same room libs, same tool registry format) so an identity can be worked from either residence without forking its memory. M5 dogfood: roerick's real workflow (todo + notes + book) run partly by agent-prickle for a week; the loop earns or loses its budget in public.")
  (implements "borge/agent.borg" "borge/local-first.borg")
   (status planned)
   (* agent note (|2026-09-08 M4 PoC SHIPPED on vultr.guest (gregor's box), ahead of the residence split: /home/al/glochid/glochid.lisp, SBCL --script daemon, zero deps, log + README beside it. Substrate: open space cactus (owner gregor); types glochid-call / glochid-result / glochid-node admitted. Calls append-only; answers are separate result rows keyed by the call row id - idempotent, restart-safe, no cross-author writes, no cursor state. Tools: shell (30s watchdog built inside sh with file capture - timeout(1) is unusable spawned from SBCL, setpgid EPERM) and fs.read (8KiB cap, secret-path deny). ACL default-deny in tiers: roerick/gregor full, agent-prickle shell-prefix allowlist + fs.read; PoC trusts the caller-written from field, so real per-identity ACL needs data_rows.author exposed in prim reads (open ask for the prim seam). VERIFIED end-to-end with prickle's own token: uptime executed (exit=0, load output intact), ls denied, env-gregor read denied, sleep 45 killed at 30s exit=137; glochid-node heartbeat fresh, answered calls skipped on every tick. Transport still /api/eval Bearer; swap to /api/prim when it ships. Run: sbcl --script /home/al/glochid/glochid.lisp|) *)
   (verify
    (smoke "one identity, two residences: glochid posts to a room, the native agent answers in the same transcript, both see identical history"))
   (* agent note (|2026-09-08 LOCKDOWN (same day, roerick: "lets lock it down"): transport moved from the open cactus to MEMBER-GATED cactus-ops (members gregor, roerick, agent-prickle) by re-admitting the glochid-* types - type routing moves with the latest space-admit, so no code change; demo rows in the open space were deleted, but the old glochid-node row could NOT be deleted by API: (delete) on a space datum is RLS-blocked by the delete-by-id hole fix and returns VNil, so the stale row sits frozen in open cactus pending admin cleanup (open kernel question: no user path deletes a space datum, not even its author). Node now runs DISARMED by default: local arm switch /home/al/glochid/.armed holds an expiry epoch (sbcl --script glochid.lisp arm [hours] / disarm); disarmed ticks heartbeat only and leave calls pending; arming drains the queue; state transitions logged. @reboot cron starts the daemon at boot, disarmed. Also fixed an fd leak (run-program streams/process never closed -> Too many open files after ~1h) and heartbeat now filters gen="2" rows only. Verified: disarmed call posted -> no result; arm 1 -> queued call executed; disarm -> locked; prickle sees the member-gated node row. STILL OPEN: from-field forgeable until prims expose author; glochid-vultr dedicated identity (M2 provisioning); /api/prim swap.|) *)
  )

 (verify
  (build "dune build @all — exit 0 (lisp + common + image)")
  (test "dune runtest — no regressions in auth, jobs, api_prim, branch_generation suites")
  (smoke "habitat: agent-wake cron fires on schedule; CRON-OK row in agent-lab; quiet tick costs no provider call (re-run of the 09-03 verification after S1/S2)"))
)